		{
			"id": "tupO02AixTheQ28NQ",
			"name": "Animal Companion",
			"local_notes": "Loyal raven with its own stats, acting under GM control; may fight, scout, track, distract, or carry objects and messages. +1 to melee attacks while it is adjacent and engaged with the same foe. If it dies, the advantage and its 5 points are lost until the GM allows a new bond.",
			"base_points": 5,
			"calc": {
				"points": 5
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "tt5HgJ36WUYGLJ19R",
			"name": "Warg Dreams",
			"local_notes": "Each night roll 1d6; on a 6 you slip into the raven. Quick Contest of Will: win and you control it (its body, your mind); lose and you only ride along behind its eyes. Return on a Will-4 roll, retried hourly or when someone shakes you awake; a Major Wound to the bird ends it and costs 1 FP. Will-4 after each episode or -1 to Influence rolls until a full night's sleep. Die while bonded and a fragment of you passes into the raven (+1 IQ, your attachments).",
			"base_points": 5,
			"calc": {
				"points": 5
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "txT8V1Xwh4Wreh4Cf",
			"source": {
				"library": "richardwilkes/gcs_master_library",
				"path": "Basic Set/Basic Set Traits.adq",
				"id": "tmp8yecgaZq9TOk59"
			},
			"name": "@Type@ Rank",
			"reference": "B29",
			"local_notes": "Rank 1 = Menkhu (line-knower), one of some two hundred. Yargachin (priest) is Rank 2 and costs 5 more - that is what the cut buys, and it is deferred, not refused. Full value in the Neck; Social Engineering p.16 -1/3 outside it. B29-30",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Social"
			],
			"replacements": {
				"Type": "Religious"
			},
			"modifiers": [
