		},
		{
			"id": "tmNZXTjZL2nIXpbkV",
			"name": "Grip Mastery (Spear)",
			"reference": "MA50",
			"local_notes": "Free action, once per turn, before or after the maneuver: shift the spear between one- and two-handed grips, and/or into or out of a Defensive Grip (MA109-111). Buys the two-handed thrust (1d+1 imp instead of 1d, tripled at the vitals) and a standing +1 to Parry from the front, without ever spending a Ready. Does NOT cover the reach change - the * in the spear's Reach 1-2* is a separate Ready option (MA102). Specialised by weapon, so it does nothing for the bow, and nothing for the bow-to-spear swap; that is still Fast-Draw (Spear). DEPENDS on the buckler being strapped to the forearm rather than hand-gripped - RAW a buckler occupies a hand (B287) and this perk would be dead weight. Precedent for the strap: LTC2 p.19. Precedent for the perk on a spear fighter: MA Gladiators p.14, retiarius.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Perk"
			],
			"base_points": 1,
			"calc": {
				"points": 1
			}
		},
