				"id": "t9CbY1uCmgSV0FolN"
			},
			"name": "Disciplines of Faith (Ritualism)",
			"reference": "B132",
			"local_notes": "The first yasakh: nothing whole. He may put nothing into his body that has not been opened first by his own hand. The second yasakh (he may not eat the beast he opened, at the Ashkun) binds the officiant at the Qanyarga and is dormant until he is Yargachin. B132",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental"
