						"weight": "0 lb",
						"extended_weight": "0 lb"
					}
				},
				{
					"id": "eV5VApxpWKHkXCuu2",
					"description": "Horn-tip and tooth on a cord",
					"local_notes": "One horn from a Qanyarga, one tooth from a Külyarga. Nineteen years old, standing among men who sound like a bone-yard in a wind. Men count them before they speak.",
					"legality_class": "4",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true,
					"calc": {
						"value": 0,
						"extended_value": 0,
						"weight": "0 lb",
						"extended_weight": "0 lb"
					}
				}
			],
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "ed3RQvtTljPJkjcih",
			"description": "Yarqap",
			"local_notes": "Splitting-vessel — the hide roll of knapped stone tashyar he intends to cut himself with at Umakhtamar. Stone rather than bronze is practice, not prohibition; the metal ban was never law. ~1 lb.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "ecXIHnn7j2OcBXw2Q",
			"description": "The Bosbash",
			"local_notes": "the aurochs-skull mask, cracked across the left orbit. Custom, no weight worth tracking\n\nIssued, not owned — masks belong to the office. Under it he is not Störm but Turkes, and what he says cannot be held against him afterward.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "eHCf-pmaPqB-J35Iy",
			"description": "The maggot-horn",
			"local_notes": "Used to clean rot out of a wound that has already gone bad. The maggots eat dead flesh and stop at living flesh, which no blade can be trusted to do. Needs four days' notice to breed a fresh batch.\n\nA lidded ox horn, kept damp, kept away from the food, never opened upwind. Blown on purpose by bog-flies onto a scrap of liver.\n\nNothing he carries is more orthodox — they open, and they are incapable of closing — and nothing empties a southern tent faster. Southerners let him do it exactly once.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_weight": "0.1 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0.1 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0.1 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "e92vJM9iRyA0tt1Pn",
			"description": "Cupping horn",
			"local_notes": "Used to draw blood and fluid up to the surface: deep bruising, a chest that will not clear, an abscess that will not come up. Warmed and set on the skin. Leeches do the same work wherever there is standing water.\n\nA small ox horn with the tip cut open. A bruise raised on purpose over a deeper hurt.\n\nDrawing out is the whole of his medicine. Everything he does to a body he can name; what the body does afterwards is the body's business, and he has decided, privately and without asking anyone, that it is not his.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_weight": "0.15 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0.15 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0.15 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "e_BE4G60dIGRD2zOr",
			"description": "Burnisher and tine",
			"local_notes": "Used to put the edge back on bronze and to press stone tools sharp again. Bronze is cold-worked hard with the pebble, not ground; the antler tine pressure-flakes stone.\n\nA smooth river pebble and an antler tine, in one fold of hide.\n\nThe tine is for the other roll. Every night he takes out the tashyar (stone-splitter) he has not used, presses the edges up sharper than anything in the kesqap (cutting-vessel), and puts them away.\n\nThe quirk 'Rehearses the cut' has a physical object. This is it.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_weight": "0.15 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0.15 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0.15 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "eOzkq7i5uESG2IgrE",
			"description": "Arrow-kit",
			"local_notes": "Used to straighten warped shafts, replace lost fletching, and reseat heads that have worked loose. Keeps thirty-five arrows flying true.\n\nAn antler shaft-wrench, spare fletching in gut, sinew, and a small pot of pine pitch kept hard and warmed at the fire.\n\nThirty-five barbed heads are thirty-five things nobody sells him. He straightens and refletches most evenings he is not doing something else, which is most evenings. A shaft that flies wide is a dose of belladonna lost in the mud.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_weight": "0.2 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0.2 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0.2 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "eAk7sfRykryjtPQIn",
			"description": "Needle-case, thongs, grease",
			"local_notes": "Used to mend and waterproof clothing, boots and hood. The tallow keeps hide and wool from rotting through; the wood-ash and stale water strips wool that has gone foul.\n\nA bird-bone tube stoppered with wax: bone needles, sinew thread, spare hide thongs. A horn of rendered tallow beside it.\n\nHooded hide over wool that has been wet for a decade does not last a decade unattended. He greases it the way other men clean armour, and he is exact about it, and it still smells like the bog, because that is what it is.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_weight": "0.2 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0.2 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0.2 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "eBHGQMAC8L2oupdq-",
			"description": "Poison doses in sealed gut",
			"local_notes": "belladonna and viper venom (5/5)\n\nBelladonna allows no resistance roll on its first cycle. One dose per strike, or three blocked or parried; one per arrow. It only fires if the attack gets through DR.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_weight": "0.1",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0.2 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0.2 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "eIAv7qjq-oZoFc4sF",
			"description": "Bog moss, and the herb-gut under it",
			"local_notes": "Used to pack and cover a dressed wound. The moss absorbs and keeps the wound sweet for a day and a night; the willow bark under it is chewed for pain and fever, the bog myrtle burned or rubbed on against flies. A Naturalist roll replaces the whole bag anywhere there is standing water.\n\nSphagnum, dried, in a net bag that weighs nothing and drinks four times its own weight.\n\nAll three grow within a mile of anywhere he has ever slept. It is the only medicine he owns that he has never had to ask a living man for, and he is unsentimental about the rest for exactly that reason.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_weight": "0.2 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0.2 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0.2 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "eB4dAPtwP9Cm7JhgX",
			"description": "Yarilmaz — honey, sealed in gut",
			"local_notes": "Used to dress an open wound, laid on after the wine and under the moss. Does not spoil, ever, and so is the one medicine that keeps as long as the road does.\n\nThat-which-will-not-open. A hand's weight of it, going brown.\n\nIt does not rot, does not sour, does not part. A vessel of it opened after a hundred years is still honey — the most whole thing he has ever handled, and the best thing in the world to lay on an opened wound. He has never resolved that, and he does not raise it.\n\nUnder the 1st yasakh nothing whole enters him unopened, so every dose is cut with water or sour wine first, aloud, by name, before it touches a patient or his own mouth. It takes him longer than it takes anybody else. The men have started timing it.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_weight": "0.25 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0.25 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0.25 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "eezJhld18jvPPDQbl",
			"description": "Ashtash — food-stone",
			"local_notes": "Used as travel rations. One cake is a day's walking. Keeps a season without spoiling and needs no cooking.\n\nDried eel, waterfowl and smoked hare pounded into rendered fat with bog cranberry and crowberry, pressed into cakes and wrapped in gut. Hard enough to have earned the name.\n\nUnder the 1st yasakh it cannot be eaten whole, so every cake is cut before it is eaten, always across the same line, and the halves are never laid back together on one board.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_weight": "0.25 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0.25 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0.25 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "eDtmHMcBssR1R78n2",
			"description": "Sour wine, in a stopped horn",
			"local_notes": "Used to wash a wound before anything else touches it, and to thin the honey to a working consistency. Drinkable at need.\n\nTraded up out of the south and worth more than his knife.\n\nIt goes onto the wound first and it bites, and the biting is the point: it opens where it lands. What is left cuts the honey. What is left after that is drunk in mouthfuls too small to be hospitality.\n\nThe only medicine in the roll his doctrine has never had to argue with.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_weight": "0.4 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0.4 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0.4 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "ej4fnujjvNojkOOEO",
			"description": "Bow-case, spare strings, wax",
			"local_notes": "Used to keep the reflex bow dry and to replace a string that has stretched or parted. Three spares. A composite bow left wet comes apart at the glue and cannot be repaired in the field.\n\nA greased hide sleeve. In a fold of it, three strings of twisted sinew carried against his skin under the wool where they stay dry, and a lump of beeswax cut with tallow to dress them.\n\nA reflex bow is horn and sinew laid up with hide glue, and hide glue dissolves in water, and he lives in a bog. It comes out to be strung and goes back the moment it is not wanted. He watched a better bow than his come apart over one wet autumn and has not been casual since.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_weight": "0.4 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0.4 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0.4 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "elJehlDIKtfrccwbt",
			"description": "Kesqap",
			"local_notes": "Used to cut, probe, stitch and dress a living body. This is the surgical kit: without one, Surgery and Esoteric Medicine are improvised at -2 or worse (B424). It grants no bonus — its absence is the penalty.\n\nCutting-vessel, and not the yarqap (splitting-vessel). Bronze lancets, a bronze probe, a horn spoon, bone needles, sinew, boiled linen in a coil.\n\nBronze, because a bronze edge can be burnished hard again on a river stone in the field and knapped stone cannot be re-struck by firelight. The stone in the yarqap is for himself and has never touched anyone. This roll is for everyone else, and is opened most days.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_weight": "0.45 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0.45 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0.45 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "e1e3zLMiOETupnfwP",
			"description": "Quivers",
			"reference": "B289",
			"local_notes": "(10 Arrows)\n\nArrows he can reach without looking. Poisoned one at a time and kept apart, because a dose on the wrong shaft is a dose gone. Barbed - causes half the damage it took coming in when taken out.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_weight": "0.5 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0.5 lb",
				"extended_weight": "0.5 lb"
			}
		},
