	"other_equipment": [
		{
			"id": "Ekb27Az5KUlErsNLy",
			"description": "Oequipment Container",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "eg3N2rlmOKk5_0XoM",
					"description": "Antler comb",
					"local_notes": "Used to comb out lice, and to dress his hair before walking into a camp that is not his.\n\nSix teeth, two of them replacements.\n\nA priest who arrives with his hair in ropes is a bog savage carrying a spear, and the office is worth more than his comfort. He combs at the tree line, before he is seen, not after.",
					"legality_class": "4",
					"base_weight": "0.05 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true,
					"calc": {
						"value": 0,
						"extended_value": 0,
						"weight": "0.05 lb",
						"extended_weight": "0.05 lb"
					}
				},
				{
					"id": "eirlAZQ6Sr_rn1z1j",
					"description": "The heavy roll",
					"local_notes": "Used for surgery that needs a fire, a table and an hour: amputation, deep extraction, setting bone, sealing a bleed the linen will not stop. Too heavy and too slow for anything that happens on the track.\n\nA bronze cautery rod, a small bow-saw for bone, split-cane splints, boiled linen by the yard, and a bronze bowl for catching what comes out.\n\nThe kesqap (cutting-vessel) on his hip is for what happens on the road. This is for what happens afterwards.\n\nThe cautery is in it and he dislikes that it is. A searing iron closes, and closing is the direction the world is not meant to travel. He has used it four times and named it aloud each time, which is not a rite anyone taught him either.",
					"legality_class": "4",
					"base_weight": "8 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true,
					"calc": {
						"value": 0,
						"extended_value": 0,
						"weight": "8 lb",
						"extended_weight": "8 lb"
					}
				}
			],
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "0 lb",
				"extended_weight": "8.05 lb"
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "esXbdQMVTukOfBaWa",
			"description": "The stores",
			"local_notes": "Used to refill the day-kit and the ration pouch. Bulk honey, wine, fat, salt and cakes against the remainder of the road — roughly forty days at current rate.\n\nHoney in a sealed crock, a skin of sour wine, bog butter lifted out of the peat where it was buried a year ago and gone tangy, salt, and a sack of ashtash (food-stone).\n\nWhat is on him is the day. This is the forty days.\n\nIt is not his. A priest cannot own or bequeath, and everything reverts to the grove, so drawing on it is an ulush (share / standing / worth) question — settled publicly, at the fire, and not by him.",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_weight": "30 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"calc": {
				"value": 0,
				"extended_value": 0,
				"weight": "30 lb",
				"extended_weight": "30 lb"
			}
		}
	],
	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "n1sRyf8TbFfiovjAo",
			"markdown": "**TRANCE — the technologies of the sacred**\n\nHow the Menkhu (line-knower) puts a mind under, and what comes back. Costs no points: every roll below is a skill he already owns.",
			"reference": "LTC1:16"
		}
	],
